      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexandria%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "When Kenton County split from Campbell County in 1840, the state assembly moved the county seat from Newport to Alexandria, placing it closer to the new county’s center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexandria%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Old Campbell County Courthouse, built in the 19th century, remains a key landmark that anchors Alexandria’s role as a county seat.",
